LibRaw 0.22.2: lossy_dng_load_raw() fills its tone-curve table cur[4][256]
only when there is no OpcodeList2 or a PolynomialMap opcode fills it. A
lossy (JPEG) DNG with an OpcodeList2 that has no PolynomialMap copies
uninitialised stack into the output pixels.

Backport of LibRaw 62f7098 (issue #862, in 0.22.3), unchanged: the default
curve is filled first, opcodes refine it. Separate from our GainMap
(patches/0006), which reads OpcodeList2 bytes and never touches this table.

--- a/src/decoders/dng.cpp
+++ b/src/decoders/dng.cpp
@@ -257,6 +257,12 @@
   ushort cur[4][256];
   double coeff[9], tot;
 
+  // Initialize the whole curve table with the default gamma curve first:
+  // an OpcodeList2 tag (meta_offset) carrying zero opcodes, or none of type
+  // PolynomialMap(8), must not leave cur[][] uninitialized.
+  gamma_curve(1 / 2.4, 12.92, 1, 255);
+  FORC4 memcpy(cur[c], curve, sizeof cur[0]);
+
   if (meta_offset)
   {
     fseek(ifp, meta_offset, SEEK_SET);
@@ -289,11 +295,6 @@
     }
     order = sorder;
   }
-  else
-  {
-    gamma_curve(1 / 2.4, 12.92, 1, 255);
-    FORC4 memcpy(cur[c], curve, sizeof cur[0]);
-  }
 
   struct jpeg_error_mgr pub;
   cinfo.err = jpeg_std_error(&pub);
